# 08 — SIR epidemic: three stocks in a flow-through chain.
# People move S → I → R. The infection flow couples Susceptible and Infected:
# reinforcing early (more infected ⇒ more infections), then balancing as the
# susceptible pool runs dry. The classic epidemic curve.
stock S [people] = 990
stock I [people] = 10
stock R [people] = 0

param beta  = 0.4      # infectiousness
param gamma = 0.1      # recovery rate
param N     = 1000     # total population

flow infection = beta * S * I / N
flow recovery  = gamma * I

change(S) = -infection
change(I) =  infection - recovery
change(R) =  recovery

sim dt=0.25 to=120 method=rk4
plot S, I, R
